# NASAQ server configuration — copy to `.env` for local work (never commit `.env`).
#
# Every variable the code reads is declared here; `npm run env:audit` fails when a
# variable is read but undocumented, or when a credential-shaped name is exposed
# with the public `VITE_` prefix. The full audit (including which variables are
# REQUIRED in production vs development) lives in `docs/environment.md`.
#
# Categories in this file:
#   1. Required in production      4. Server-only secrets
#   2. Required in development     5. Public / client variables
#   3. Optional
#
# Rules that are not negotiable:
#   · never put a real secret in this file or anywhere in Git;
#   · never prefix a secret with VITE_ — those are inlined into the browser bundle.

# ═══ 1. Required in production (Vercel) ══════════════════════════════════════

# Accounts and sessions are served by this app's own Better Auth at /api/auth/*.
# `false` disables sign-in entirely (local-only mode); production keeps it `true`.
VITE_AUTH_ENABLED=true

# Session signing secret. MUST be a freshly generated random value used NOWHERE
# else — never the same string as GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET or any API key.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32     (at least 32 characters)
# Without it on a deployment, sessions are signed with a per-process random value
# and the visitor is signed out again on the next request; the app reports this
# loudly at boot and on /login instead of failing silently.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Managed Postgres (free Neon works). Vercel functions have no writable
# filesystem, so the embedded PGLite fallback cannot run there. Migrations apply
# automatically during `npm run build`.
DATABASE_URL=

# Canonical public origin. Used for the Google OAuth redirect URI and as the
# Better Auth base URL. Every other host this deployment answers on (Vercel
# platform URL, preview URLs, custom domains) is trusted automatically; add more
# with NASAQ_TRUSTED_ORIGINS below.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://nasaq-sa.vercel.app

# ═══ 2. Required in development (optional in production) ════════════════════
# Local work runs on the embedded PGLite database with a per-process signing
# secret, so none of the above is needed to run `npm run dev`. Set
# `VITE_AUTH_ENABLED=false` only for a local-only session with no accounts at all.

# ═══ 3. Optional ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Google sign-in (optional — email/password needs no provider). Both values are
# required to enable the provider; a server-only client secret, kept out of Vite.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Google Cloud → Credentials → Web OAuth client. A DIFFERENT secret from
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET; reusing one value for both is a misconfiguration the app
# reports as a blocking error.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Public origin used by owner diagnostics (Ping self-test). Falls back to
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL / BETTER_AUTH_URL when unset.
# NASAQ_PUBLIC_URL=https://nasaq-sa.vercel.app

# Extra origins (and wildcard patterns) allowed to POST credentials to this app.
# Comma-separated. Bare hosts are trusted on both http and https.
# Example: NASAQ_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://nasaq.app,*.nasaq.sa
NASAQ_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=

# Extra host patterns accepted by Better Auth's per-request base URL.
# Example: NASAQ_ALLOWED_HOSTS=staging.nasaq.app
NASAQ_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# Force the production requirements (BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, DATABASE_URL, https
# origin) on a self-hosted runtime that does not set VERCEL=1.
# NASAQ_STRICT_ENV=1

# AI provider (Gemini). Server-only: read in `src/lib/ai/provider.server.ts`.
# Without it every AI surface answers "not_configured" — clearly, never silently.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
NASAQ_AI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ── Gumroad — the ONLY payment provider (memberships) ───────────────────────
# Keygen is the licensing authority.
# Live product: https://nasaqar.gumroad.com/l/auaewk (tiers نَسَق | فردي / فريق).
# Server-only: used to verify every sale/subscription before Keygen issuance.
#
# How to obtain it (one-time, no OAuth for users):
#   Gumroad → Settings → Advanced → Applications → Create application
#     Application name: NASAQ — نَسَق (تكامل الخادم)
#     Redirect URI:     http://127.0.0.1   ← required by Gumroad's form only;
#                       its value is never used by NASAQ (no redirect handler,
#                       no per-user sign-in flow exists in this codebase).
#     Application icon: optional — leave empty.
#   Then: Your applications → Edit → Generate access token → copy the value here.
# The Application ID / Application Secret are NOT used and must not be stored.
GUMROAD_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Product id (from the license-key block on the product page or GET /v2/products).
# OPTIONAL: with GUMROAD_ACCESS_TOKEN set, the product id is resolved
# automatically from GET /v2/products by matching GUMROAD_PRODUCT_PERMALINK
# (see resolveGumroadProductId in src/lib/gumroad/config.server.ts). Set it
# explicitly only to pin a product when the store hosts more than one.
GUMROAD_PRODUCT_ID=
GUMROAD_PRODUCT_PERMALINK=auaewk
GUMROAD_STORE_BASE_URL=https://nasaqar.gumroad.com
# Optional overrides — pin the exact Gumroad tier names if they are ever renamed.
# Defaults: نَسَق | فردي / نَسَق | فريق
GUMROAD_TIER_INDIVIDUAL_NAME=
GUMROAD_TIER_TEAM_NAME=

# Register the post-sale Ping / Resource subscriptions in Gumroad →
# Settings → Advanced as:  https://nasaq-sa.vercel.app/api/webhooks/gumroad
KEYGEN_ACCOUNT_SLUG=ararcomksa-twilight-fire-2288
KEYGEN_PRODUCT_ID=c109271b-9c97-4827-bc9d-48e7982744fe
# Product token permissions: entitlement.read, license.read, license.create,
# license.update, license.suspend, license.reinstate, user.read, user.create,
# license.users.attach (needed to bind an unassigned user-locked key on activation).
# Keep this token server-only; a token with only license.create cannot claim keys.
KEYGEN_API_TOKEN=
# Ed25519 hexadecimal verify key from Keygen Developers settings.
KEYGEN_PUBLIC_KEY=
KEYGEN_POLICY_TRIAL_ID=ab6e0fdd-7e5e-4329-afe1-6c9e6b92acb7
KEYGEN_POLICY_INDIVIDUAL_MONTHLY_ID=e9bea931-5416-4a91-95f8-8a90b26a2cd6
KEYGEN_POLICY_INDIVIDUAL_QUARTERLY_ID=7b078b25-8fd0-485d-9dd6-75b92afb24c9
KEYGEN_POLICY_TEAM_MONTHLY_ID=2b6984ed-1022-4718-a0b3-cc07c4cd5dad
KEYGEN_POLICY_TEAM_QUARTERLY_ID=6a4b079a-45f8-4e94-90a6-b8864acbfd96
KEYGEN_POLICY_LIFETIME_ID=3704e4a4-5645-4be7-b6c9-2067c722341d

# The Better Auth `user.id` of the owner account (read it from the deployed
# database after the owner signs in once) and/or the owner's verified email.
# Either one alone is enough; the email is the easier value to fill in first.
# With email/password enabled, an owner can now be identified by the address they
# registered with — no Google account is required.
NASAQ_OWNER_ID=
NASAQ_OWNER_EMAIL=
# Owner bypass for licence administration (SUPER_ADMIN). Accepts verified user
# ids and/or email addresses, comma-separated. The owner record above is always
# treated as a super administrator, with or without these.
NASAQ_SUPER_ADMIN_IDS=
NASAQ_SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS=
# Optional explicit admin allowlist: comma-separated verified user IDs and/or emails.
# Admin identities receive full access without a paid subscription.
NASAQ_ADMIN_USER_IDS=

# ── Cloudflare R2 object storage (S3-compatible) ─────────────────────────
# Optional: with these unset the editor keeps its local-first asset library
# and every storage call returns "not_configured" instead of failing.
# R2_ENDPOINT wins when set; otherwise the endpoint is derived from the
# account id as https://<R2_ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# The secret is server-only — never prefix any of these with VITE_.
# The R2 API token needs Object Read & Write on the bucket (upload, read and
# signed URL, delete). Verify activation with `npm run storage:verify`, which
# reports missing variable NAMES only and runs the full round trip.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_NAME=nasaq-sa
R2_ENDPOINT=

# ── Image enhancement (editor: إزالة الخلفية / الضجيج / الترقية) ──────────
# All three image tools run LOCALLY in the user's browser — no image bytes are
# ever uploaded and no server key is required. The upscaling model (ESRGAN ×4)
# is vendored same-origin at build time. Only the background-removal model
# weights stream once from the model CDN; to self-host them instead, point
# this at your own copy of @imgly/background-removal-data's dist/. Optional —
# leave empty to use the default CDN. No secret is ever exposed to the client.
# VITE_NASAQ_BG_MODEL_PUBLIC_PATH=

# ── Optional: unset on purpose ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is read by the code but is NOT required by the Vercel
# production deployment. Leave empty unless the matching capability is wanted.
#
# Grok platform gate. Injected by the Grok deployer only; on Vercel the app
# signs in through Better Auth instead, so these stay unset and
# `isWorkspacePreview()` correctly keeps the gate/connector paths inert.
# GROK_PROJECT_ID=
# GROK_GATE_ORIGIN=
# GROK_CONNECTORS_URL=
# GROK_CONNECTOR_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Public hostname used only by the PWA manifest scripts on Grok-published apps.
# VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTNAME=
# Comma-separated STUN servers for P2P collaboration; defaults to Google STUN.
# VITE_STUN_URLS=
# Sample licence key for scripts/license-compat-check.mjs only.
# NASAQ_COMPAT_KEY=
#
# Not integrated at all (no email, analytics, monitoring or Grok connectors
# are wired into the product): nothing to configure.
#
# ── 5. Public / client variables (inlined into the browser bundle) ────────
# Only VITE_* names are visible to the browser, and ONLY non-secret values may
# carry that prefix: VITE_AUTH_ENABLED, VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTNAME, VITE_STUN_URLS,
# VITE_NASAQ_BG_MODEL_PUBLIC_PATH. Everything else in this file is server-only.
